World origin shift

Adds b3World_ShiftOrigin( worldId, newOrigin ), which moves the world origin in
one pass so that position -= newOrigin for everything the world stores in
world space: the transform, center and previous center of every body sim in
every solver set (static, disabled, awake and each sleeping island), the tight
and fat bounding box of every shape, the leaves of the three broad-phase trees,
whose internal nodes are then recomputed as the union of their leaves, the
cached query box of every mesh contact, and the body move and contact hit
events of the last step.

Joint frames, contact manifolds, warm starting impulses, contact recycling
poses and velocities are relative to the bodies and do not change. No body is
woken, no proxy is marked as moved, and no tree is rebuilt, so a resting or
sleeping island stays as it is and the next step creates no new pairs. Fat
boxes are shifted with outward rounding and then grown to the recomputed tight
box, so a proxy never stops enclosing its shape. A mesh contact's query box is
emptied, so its next update queries the triangles again and keeps the caches
of the triangles it finds again.

The shift is refused while the world is locked and ignored for a non-finite
origin. It is recorded as op 0x71, and the recording minor version becomes 11.

